 ## Overview
-This method loads LLFF-style datasets, corrects coordinate system conventions, rescales poses and bounds, and generates a spiral camera path for novel view synthesis [S1, unofficial]. It differs from sibling preprocessing methods by specifically handling the axis-flip correction required for LLFF data and constructing the parametric spiral trajectory used for testing [S1, unofficial].
+This method prepares LLFF-style datasets for NeRF training by loading poses and images, applying geometric normalization, and generating a spiral render path for novel view synthesis. It differs from standard loading by explicitly handling the minification step via external tools and enforcing a specific train/test split protocol (every 8th image for testing) [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs:**
